          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "o direito — \"the right; law (as a subject)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Todas as crianças têm direito à educação. All children have a right to education."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ter direito a — to have a right to. Estudar Direito — to study law. Also the adjective right: a mão direita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "direito is inherited from Latin dīrēctus \"straight\", the participle of dīrigere \"to set straight\" (Lewis & Short), built on regere \"to guide, to rule\"; -ct- became -it- as in feito."
            }
          ]
        },
